cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PyGeoParallax-IN: cloud parallax correction for INSAT-3DR imagery over India"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python tool that corrects INSAT-3DR geostationary imagery for cloud
  parallax by ray tracing on the WGS84 ellipsoid (optionally with terrain), applies a
  navigation correction measured from coastlines, and writes uncorrected and corrected
  datasets on the same grid. Includes readers for INSAT-3DR L1C/L2B, GPM 2A Ku, ERA5
  and SRTM, and validation tools against GPM radar.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bapalli
    given-names: Naveen
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23666957
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bapallinaveen60/PyGeoParallax-IN"
keywords:
  - parallax correction
  - INSAT-3DR
  - geostationary satellite
  - navigation
  - GPM
  - Indian monsoon
